"P3486166729" "Powers at Play"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - KingSpared 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P705671635" "Clockwork Mercy"
// DetailString :
"P494553546" "You took pity on the Clockwork King, and forgave his misguided actions. He let Penelope return to Phalanx HQ without causing any more trouble."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - KingFought 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3133815051" "Clockwork Vengeance"
// DetailString :
"P2332491068" "You showed no mercy to the Clockwork King. Even when he no longer wished to fight, you made sure he knew the consequences of attacking the heroes of Paragon City."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PandorasBoxHeroArc1Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3138190341" "Glowing Shrapnel"
// tDetailString :
"P2650822824" "This jagged piece of metal still hums with a strange energy - the same power that allowed Clamor to challenge the Freedom Phalanx itself. You find yourself wondering Clamor had a hand in her own empowerment, or if she was just a pawn of...<br><br><color gold><b>Powers at Play</b></color><br><br>When Wavelength originally requested that you assist the Phalanx in their duties, you knew you'd be taking on a heavy responsibility - just not quite so abruptly. During your meeting with the Positron, the Clockwork King sent his minions to attack, and whisked away the newest member, Penelope Yin. The Phalanx split up to pursue the fleeing Clockwork, but you managed to track down their escape to a warehouse in Atlas Park. There, you found the Clockwork King and Penelope in the middle of a heated argument, but Penelope seemed to be safe from any immediate danger.<br><br>Unfortunately, after leaving the warehouse, Wavelength informed you that Positron and Numina had been ambushed during their search of Skyway City. The local Superadine-empowered gang, the Trolls, had somehow managed to overpower them, and Wavelength requested your assistance. You rushed to Skyway and rescued both Positron and Numina, and faced down the Trolls' leader, Atta. The trolls in Skyway seemed to be empowered by something beyond their drugs... as though an external force had granted them tremendous power.<br><br>Upon returning to Fort Trident, you met with the Freedom Phalanx, who were recovering from their battle and investigating the source of the strange energy that empowered the Trolls. Citadel detected a similar energy surge near City Hall, and Positron asked you to investigate. When you emerged from Fort Trident, you found City Hall being attacked by the Talons of Vengeance and their Freakshow allies. Their ringleader appeared to be Clamor, who had joined with the Talons and was empowered with the same energy as the Trolls. After defeating Clamor, the Freedom Phalanx joined you in her interrogation, and Penelope Yin managed to extract crucial information from her: the source of her empowerment was the ancient mythological artifact called Pandora's Box."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - PositronTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P2524136647" "Ah. {HeroName}. I see that Wavelength managed to get in contact with you."
// Answer Text :
"P3495107274" "What's going on?"
// Page What Text :
"P4065238349" "<color orange>Positron nods towards the Phalanx's newest member.</color><br><br>Ms. Yin has been using her psychic powers to pull 'pranks' on her teammates. She does not seem to understand that mental domination is no laughing matter.<br><br><color orange>He turns his attention back to Penelope.</color><br><br>Responsible use of powers is what separates Heroes from our adversaries. Using them recklessly will only cause the people of Paragon to mistrust us."
// Answer Text :
"P3418888479" "I... see."
// Page What2 Text :
"P406125052" "<img align=left src=costume:Model_Penelope_Yin_New width=128 height=128>I said I was <b><i>sorry</b></i>, ok? Besides, Justin had it coming. Guy's had it out for me ever since I joined."
// Answer Text :
"P832514951" "Right..."
// Page What3 Text :
"P3690360666" "Both of you need to calm down. We are the <b><i>Freedom Phalanx</b></i>, people. We need to be the ones to set an example. Bickering amongst ourselves is counterproductive.<br><br><color orange>Positron returns his attention to you.</color><br><br>I apologize for this, {HeroName}. Statesman's death has hit the group hard, and we're stretched pretty thin right now."
// Answer Text :
"P2117863612" "Yes, Wavelength said as much."
// Page HasSouvenir Text :
"P2434868485" "<color orange>Positron nods slowly.</color><br><br>The Phalanx is undergoing some... organizational restructuring, and we're not exactly at peak efficiency at the moment. We've put a call out to some of the more veteran heroes in Paragon for assistance during the transition. Your work in stopping Darrin Wade made you an obvious choice.<br><br><color orange>Positron extends his hand to you.</color><br><br>Well, {HeroName}? What do you say? The Phalanx is in need of your help. Would you be willing to work with us?"
// Answer Text :
"P1207667763" "I would be honored, Positr-"
// Answer Text :
"P4043642947" "I'm sorry, but I work alo-"
// Page NoSouvenir Text :
"P273163232" "<color orange>Positron nods slowly.</color><br><br>The Phalanx is undergoing some... organizational restructuring, and we're not exactly at peak efficiency at the moment. We've put a call out to some of the more veteran heroes in Paragon for assistance during the transition. I've been following your work in Paragon for some time now, and you seemed an obvious choice.<br><br><color orange>Positron extends his hand to you.</color><br><br>Well, {HeroName}? What do you say? The Phalanx is in need of your help. Would you be willing to work with us?"
// Page AfterFight Text :
"P1062264413" "Keep an eye out, people. Citadel, what's our security status?"
// Answer Text :
"P1450575615" "(Listen to Citadel)"
// Page AfterFight2 Text :
"P1943819508" "<img align=left src=costume:Model_Bastion_NoRing width=128 height=128>Patching into the system now.<br><br>All internal cameras and external sensors report no nearby hostiles. It appears we have repelled their assault. However, they have captured Penelope Yin, and I am currently unable to ascertain how the Clockwork managed to infiltrate this base."
// Answer Text :
"P2817534760" "Why would the Clockwork have an interest in Penelope?"
// Answer Text :
"P802312947" "Is there a way to track down the Clockwork King?"
// Page WhyPenelope Text :
"P4225988598" "The Clockwork King and Penelope have a... complicated history. He's been obsessed with her for years... I believe it has something to do with their mutually potent psychic abilities, but I cannot be sure.<br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><color yellow>For more backstory on Penelope Yin and the Clockwork King, check out Mission 1 of the Lady Grey Task Force!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P4123711795" "Alright... so what do we do now?"
// Page TrackDown Text :
"P2542865770" "<img align=left src=costume:Model_Bastion_NoRing width=128 height=128>External sensors have tracked multiple groups of Clockwork exiting the base perimeter. Unfortunately, they seem to have taken divergent routes, most likely in an attempt to prevent pursuit."
// Answer Text :
"P1183400229" "Great..."
// Page TrackDown2 Text :
"P4164684515" "We're going to need to split up, then. Brawler, you and Manticore follow the group headed for Perez. Citadel, Synapse, you've got Steel Canyon. Numina, you're with me - we're going to need flyers in Skyway if we want to cover ground quickly.<br><br><color orange>Positron turns to you.</color><br><br>{HeroName}, we could really use your help on this one. Can we count on you?"
// Answer Text :
"P3647817140" "I'm in."
// Page TrackDown3 Text :
"P1807277214" "Excellent. We've got enough people to pursue the Clockwork, but it occurs to me that these runners may be decoys. Make a run through Atlas Park and look for any suspicious Clockwork activity. With any luck, one of us will find where they took Penelope."
// Answer Text :
"P4262229902" "Understood."
// Page ClosePage Text :
"P856364347" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DaviesTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1207006239" "{HeroName}, good to see you. Word is you've been working with the Phalanx lately. It's a good thing, too, given what they've been going through lately.<br><br>But you probably didn't come here for small talk. What can I do for you?"
// Answer Text :
"P741192992" "I'm looking for any unusual Clockwork activity in the area."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P3152763277" "Funny you should ask that, actually. I just got a call in from a local hero that was going to bust a Clockwork salvage operation, only to end up in the hospital. Now, this guy claims the Clockwork he was fighting were way beyond what you normally see in Atlas Park, but I wrote it off as wounded pride. A lot of the younger heroes will bite off more than they can chew, and then truss up their story to save face.<br><br>Still, if you think this guy was telling the truth, I can give you the coordinates to the warehouse."
// Answer Text :
"P3403001792" "I appreciate it."
// Answer Text :
"P2384831810" "Maybe you should put more faith in the heroes of this city, Davies."
// Page Appreciate Text :
"P2555212153" "No problem, {HeroName}. I hope you find what you're looking for.<br><br>Good hunting."
// Answer Text :
"P1979365012" "See you around, Rick."
// Page Stern Text :
"P3681105881" "Whoa now, no need to get testy. I've been in the hero's shoes myself, so I know what it's like.<br><br>Tell you what, if this lead turns out to be solid, then my first stop will be to Chiron Medical to issue a formal apology. Cool?"
// Answer Text :
"P669054632" "Fine. Thanks for the tip."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - KingTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P978909120" "Please, Penny. You have to understand... everything I've done, I've done for you! Why can't you appreciate that?<br><br>Those 'heroes' in the Phalanx will never be able to protect you like I can. You have to see that!"
// Answer Text :
"P2752416947" "(Allow the conversation to continue)"
// Answer Text :
"P3095106004" "I've heard enough. I'm bringing you in, King."
// Page SoapOpera1 Text :
"P3585978869" "<img align=left src=costume:Model_Penelope_Yin_New width=128 height=128>You... you think you're <b><i>protecting</b></i> me? Russell, wake up already! I'm not some helpless little girl anymore! You've helped me in the past, and you <i>know</i> I appreciate that, but it has to end! I can take care of myself!<br><br>Look, I know how you feel about the Phalanx. I know you hate heroes, and I know you well enough to understand why.<br><br><color orange>Penelope gestures to her costume.</color><br><br>But I'm a hero now. Officially. I have a license and everything. So you can keep trying to help me, and protect me... or you can keep on hating heroes.<br><br>But you can't do both. Not anymore."
// Page SoapOpera2 Text :
"P1403408010" "<color orange>The Clockwork King hangs his... 'head'... in shame.</color><br><br>I don't want to lose you, Penelope. You're all I have left. My little... my little princess.<br><br><color orange>The Clockwork King turns to you.</color><br><br>I'm done, {HeroName}. I'll leave you and the Freedom Phalanx alone... for the moment. But I swear, if Penelope should come to harm while under your care, I will stop at <b><i>nothing</b></i> to avenge her.<br><br>But for now, I believe we have a truce."
// Answer Text :
"P3467408409" "No harm, no foul, I suppose."
// Answer Text :
"P1077225478" "Sorry, but you don't get to walk away from attacking a Phalanx facility."
// Page LetKingGo Text :
"P4214693144" "<img align=left src=costume:Model_Penelope_Yin_New width=128 height=128>Thank you for understanding, {HeroName}. Russell's a little hotheaded, but he means well.<br><br>You know... I'm kind of glad Posi asked you to help out the Phalanx. You can be pretty cool sometimes.<br><br>Anyway, I guess I'll see you back at HQ."
// Answer Text :
"P1103312093" "Alright, Penelope."
// Page FightTheKing Text :
"P3677039058" "Typical! You see, Penny? <b><i>This</b></i> is a the true nature of 'heroes'! You'll regret challenging me, {HeroName}!"
// Answer Text :
"P2896749163" "I don't find that likely."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - PennyTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P434879621" "What are you DOING, {HeroName}? He already said he'd stop attacking the Phalanx. There was absolutely <b><i>no</b></i> reason for you to attack him!"
// Answer Text :
"P4158392531" "It was justice, Penelope. Attacking registered heroes is a crime."
// Answer Text :
"P3672857506" "You may trust the Clockwork King, but I don’t."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P560863061" "Of all the twisted, messed-up... UGH!<br><br><color orange>Penelope's words choke off as she tries to make sense of what has happened.</color><br><br>You are <b>sick</b>, you know that, {HeroName}? You may think you're justified in everything you do, but in this case, you're dead wrong.<br><br><color orange>Penelope turns from you in disgust.</color><br><br>Just leave me alone. I'll head back to HQ myself, after I've made sure Russell's ok."
// Answer Text :
"P4075786299" "I'll make sure the proper authorities will be waiting for him."

